  "                             SETTING UP YOUR BOARD                            ",
  "  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────",
  "  CONFIG on its own lists the pages. CONFIG and a page name opens one:        ",
  "  CONFIG board is the first. F1 saves a page and most changes apply at once.  ",
  "                                                                              ",
  "  THE PAGES                                                                   ",
  "  board     the board's name, its hostname on the network, the timezone       ",
  "            and NTP server, idle minutes, the LED pin, where callers land     ",
  "  limits    minutes per call and per day, the WHO refresh, the account cap    ",
  "  accounts  whether callers may sign up, whether guests may call, and for     ",
  "            how many minutes                                                  ",
  "  backup    the port, how long the window stays open, the button pin          ",
  "  staff     the passwords you just set                                        ",
  "  wifi      the network; a change is used from the next restart               ",
  "                                                                              ",
  "  And one page for each plugin: chat, forums, files, info, announce           ",
  "  and sd. Each starts with whether it is on and who may use it.               ",
